1Monoallelic SNPs were dropped. Given that SAMAFS is a family study, SNP genotypes were checked for Mendelian consistency and discrepant genotypes were blanked, after which MERLIN program was used to impute missing genotypes conditional on relatives' genotypes, with a weighted average of possible genotypes being used when an individual's genotype could not be inferred with certainty.																															
2 Lamdas for Stage 2 Studies that only submitted SNPs for replication as based on their full genome-wide data results.																															
* Starr County submitted only imputed data due to complications in calling genotyped data that resulted in lower call rates. (More information available in PMID: 21647700 (PMC3761075).																															
